<h2 id="three-questions">Three questions about living costs</h2>

<ol>
  <li><strong>What do pensioner households spend?</strong> Surveys record this. Spending is limited by income, so low spending can mean going without. It does not show low need.</li>
  <li><strong>What does a minimum acceptable standard of living cost?</strong> Researchers ask groups of the public to agree a list of goods and services, then price it. The result is a benchmark.</li>
  <li><strong>What does a particular household need?</strong> That depends on housing, health, where the household lives, and who is in it. No national figure answers it.</li>
</ol>

{% call m.note("Four things these figures are not", 3) %}
<ul>
  <li>A research budget is not a legal entitlement. No benefit is set by it.</li>
  <li>Falling below a research budget is not the same as being in poverty as official statistics measure it. The two use different tests.</li>
  <li>A survey average for households is not how one person spends a State Pension.</li>
  <li>Do not assume that a household lives on the State Pension alone, or that it receives extra support automatically. Most pensioners have other income. Many who could claim Pension Credit do not.</li>
</ul>
{% endcall %}

<h2 id="research-budgets">What research says a standard of living costs</h2>

<h3 id="mis-2026">The Minimum Income Standard, 2026</h3>

<p>The Minimum Income Standard is produced by Loughborough University for the Joseph Rowntree Foundation. Groups of members of the public agree what a household needs for a minimum socially acceptable standard of living. {{ m.c("mis-not-poverty-line") }}</p>

{%- set g = ["mis-single-ex-rent", "mis-couple-ex-rent"] | shared %}
{{ m.sharedNote(g) }}
<ul class="cards">
  <li>{{ m.stat("mis-single-ex-rent" | figure, "A week, for a single pensioner, not counting rent.", 4, g) }}</li>
  <li>{{ m.stat("mis-couple-ex-rent" | figure, "A week, for a pensioner couple, not counting rent.", 4, g) }}</li>
</ul>

<p>Rent is shown separately because it differs so much by area. The budgets use an indicative private rent of {{ m.f("mis-single-rent") }} a week for a single pensioner and {{ m.f("mis-couple-rent") }} for a couple.</p>
{{ m.sourceNote("mis-single-rent" | figure) }}

{% call m.note("The 2026 budgets cannot be compared directly with earlier years", 4) %}
<p>{{ ("mis-tenure-change" | claim).statement }} {{ m.c("mis-tenure-change") }} {{ ("mis-basket-change" | claim).statement }} {{ m.c("mis-basket-change") }} A change in the benchmark from one year to the next is not only a change in prices.</p>
{% endcall %}

