<p>To compare the pension with prices, the two must cover the same period. Over five years, from April 2021 to April 2026, the full new State Pension rose from {{ (history.years | where("tax_year", "2021/22") | first).new_pence | money }} to {{ (history.years | where("tax_year", "2026/27") | first).new_pence | money }} a week. That period is close to the five years in the table but not the same, and the pension rises once a year while prices rise through the year. One inflation reading does not test whether the pension is adequate. <a href="/history/">Rates and prices over time</a>.</p>

